    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125036": {
      "title": "Assistant House Manager",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant House Manager Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant House Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. This role will report to the Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington DC. Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: Events & Venues at the George Washington University (a department in the Safety & Facilities Division) designs, produces, and manages events on the Foggy Bottom Campus. We provide services to a broad spectrum of clients both in the community and outside of the community. We provide spaces for our students, faculty, staff, and guests to host events, meetings, and gatherings. We highlight university traditions, produce memorable guest speaker events, and coordinate many other activities unique to our campus with local, national, and international acclaim. Our record of excellence, support, and cooperation is one that we are proud of. Events & Venues are seeking temporary Assistant House Managers. This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. The responsibilities for this position include but are not limited to: -Lead the Usher team and ensure the smooth running of the Front of House operations -Ensure all Front of House staff have the appropriate training including customer service and health and safety -Create staff rotations and ensure the Front of House is staffed at all times -Provide excellent customer service to all visitors of the theatre -Address any issues raised by visitors during events -Act as an emergency warden should patrons need to be removed from the venue -Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED plus 3 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Ideal candidates must have 1000 hours plus working in a theater ushering capacity II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Safety and Operation Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 20 Hiring Range $17.95/hour - $30.00/hour Work Schedule: Monday-Sunday, Occasional Evenings Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. This role will report to the Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington DC. Position Type: Posting Number: T000593 Job Open Date: 03/25/2026 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: No Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is the hourly rate you are looking to make? Please provide a range below. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129498": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Neurobiology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty applicationand upload the following documents: I. a cover letter describing qualifications and fit within the department (1 page); II. a curriculum vitae including a full list of publications and of references; III. a research statement (2 pages); IV. a teaching statement (1-2 pages); V. three recent publications; and VI. a list of names and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Please contact Dr. Damien O’Halloran at damienoh@gwu.edu, Chair of the Neuroscience Faculty Search Committee, with any questions. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002666 Academic Title: Assistant Professor in Neurobiology Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Neurobiology Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences at The George Washington University ( GWU ) invites applicants for a tenure-track faculty position in Neurobiology at the rank of Assistant Professor, to begin as early as Fall 2027. The Department of Biological Sciences brings together investigators using diverse experimental systems and cutting-edge molecular, cellular, genomic, physiological, and computational approaches to address fundamental questions in biology. The Department has broad strengths spanning neuroscience, anatomy and physiology, cell and molecular biology, immunology, developmental biology, evolution, ecology, and organismal biology. The department seeks a candidate with complementary expertise who investigates fundamental questions in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models, including but not limited to neural development and function, neurophysiology, neurobiology of behavior, neuroimmune interactions, and neural regeneration and repair . Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an externally funded research program that integrates graduate and undergraduate students and investigates basic cellular and molecular questions in neurobiology. The successful candidate will also strengthen our multidisciplinary teaching program by teaching a course in Molecular Biology and a new course for our Neuroscience major, related to the successful candidate’s area of expertise. Minimum Qualifications: Required Qualifications: (1) a completed PhD in neurobiology or a closely related field; (2) research expertise in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models; (3) at least 2 years of postdoctoral experience at the start of the position; and (4) research accomplishments as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications. Advertised Salary: $90,000-$96,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for GW’s full-time employee benefits package. For more information on GW’s benefits visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits Other Information: Abundant opportunities exist for interdisciplinary research and collaboration across the Department, the Columbian College of Arts and Sciences, the GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences, and the broader George Washington University community. The University’s location in Washington, DC provides opportunities for collaborations with federal agencies, research institutes, hospitals, and biomedical organizations, including the National Institutes of Health, the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, Children’s National Hospital, and other institutions within the region’s exceptionally strong biomedical research community. Faculty can also engage with GW’s interdisciplinary research centers and programs spanning neuroscience, biomedical sciences, computational biology, immunology, and translational medicine. The Department provides access to a diverse and accomplished community of undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, as well as opportunities to mentor trainees through GW’s interdisciplinary graduate programs. The Department of Biological Sciences is committed to building a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive intellectual community in which faculty, trainees, and staff can thrive. We value scientific innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration, excellence in teaching and mentorship, and the inclusion of diverse perspectives that strengthen our research and educational missions. Office and laboratory space will be located in GWU’s Science and Engineering Hall, a newer building on campus which opened in January 2015 ( https://www.gwu.edu/research- resources#Discovery) and offers state-of-the-art imaging and nanofabrication facilities. Our location in Washington, DC offers exceptional undergraduate and graduate mentorship opportunities through proximity to the National Institutes of Health, Janelia Research Campus, the Smithsonian Institution and a consortium of DC-area universities. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty applicationand upload the following documents: I. a cover letter describing qualifications and fit within the department (1 page); II. a curriculum vitae including a full list of publications and of references; III . a research statement (2 pages); IV. a teaching statement (1-2 pages); V. three recent publications; and VI. a list of names and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Please contact Dr. Damien O’Halloran at damienoh@gwu.edu, Chair of the Neuroscience Faculty Search Committee, with any questions. Department Link: https://biology.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129027 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Statement of Research Interest Sample Publications Names and Contact Information for References Optional Documents List of Publications Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a completed PhD in neurobiology or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have research expertise in cellular and molecular neuroscience using non-mammalian experimental models? Yes No * Will you have at least 2 years of postdoctoral experience at the time of the appointment? Yes No * Do you have research accomplishments as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129012": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions—Outpatient Psychiatrists",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions—Outpatient Psychiatrists Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions—Outpatient Psychiatrists Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002662 Academic Title: Faculty Positions—Outpatient Psychiatrists Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/1/2026-06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University and Capital Medical Group ( CMG ), formerly known as the Medical Faculty Associates, are seeking academic psychiatrists for full-time, regular faculty appointments in the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Health. These non-tenure-track positions, expected to start as early as Winter 2026, will be filled at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include conducting initial psychiatric evaluations, managing medications, and providing ongoing psychotherapy for adult patients. The psychiatrists are part of a collaborative team of academic psychiatrists, psychologists, psychiatry residents, and primary care physicians. The psychiatrists will also participate in medical student education and residency training with the potential for participation in clinical research. In addition, the psychiatrists will participate in the GWUH call coverage rotation for a 20-bed inpatient psychiatric unit, emergency room, and C/L service, including weeknight phone call and weekend/holiday call, which includes in-house rounding. The psychiatric service is covered in-house by psychiatry residents 24/7. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in General Psychiatry and license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: Salary commensurate with experience, ranging from $240,000 to $300,000. Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The Capital Medical Group also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://jobs.uhsinc.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128898 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in General Psychiatry at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120830": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions - Rheumatology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on July 17, 2025, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002535 Academic Title: Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Medicine/Rheumatology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 9/1/25-6/30/26 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 09/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) is seeking full-time academic rheumatologists to join the growing Division of Rheumatology of the Department of Medicine. The MFA is an independent, non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University and is part of a large academic health center located in the heart of the nation’s capital. These non-tenure track appointments will be made at a rank (instructor/assistant/associate/full professor) and salary commensurate with experience. These positions are expected to begin as early as Fall 2025. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing quality clinical service, engaging in effective teaching, and maintaining a productive research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Internal Medicine and Rheumatology, and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. They must also have an established record of providing excellent clinical care services, research productivity, and clinical teaching as demonstrated by experience, publications, evaluations, and/or references. Advertised Salary: $199,000.00 to $249,000.00 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on July 17, 2025, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/rheumatology Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120403 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in Internal Medicine and Rheumatology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have an established record of providing excellent clinical care services as demonstrated by experience, publications, evaluations and/or references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129287": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Geography",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Geography Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Geography Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please complete an online application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129037, uploading the following documents: Cover Letter. A current curriculum vitae (CV). A Statement of research interests. A statement of teaching interests/philosophy. Transcripts of all college work. Unofficial transcripts will suffice for the application. Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references. Reference letters may be requested later. Review of applications will begin November 12, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002670 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Geography Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Geography and Environment at the George Washington University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning as soon as Fall 2027. We seek an environmental scientist, physical geographer, or earth-system scientist whose research advances understanding of climate and environmental change and human interactions with the Earth system. Areas of interest may include biogeography, climatology, water resources, ecosystem and land-surface processes, and coupled human-environment systems. We are particularly interested in candidates who combine field research with quantitative and geospatial approaches and who will develop an externally funded research program involving undergraduate and graduate students. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach two undergraduate and/or graduate courses each semester in environmental science and physical geography, advise and mentor undergraduate and MS students, and contribute to the department’s Environmental and Sustainability Science and Geography programs. As a highly collegial department, we expect faculty to contribute actively to departmental life through advising, governance, program development, and other shared responsibilities, as well as through service to the university, the profession, and the broader community. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have a PhD in geography, environmental science, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Applicants must have demonstrated research or teaching experience using field and quantitative methods or geospatial methods. Advertised Salary: $85,000-$100,000 Other Benefits: The successful applicant will be eligible for GW’s comprehensive benefits package including employee medical insurance. For benefits details please see https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs Other Information: The Department of Geography and Environment brings together geographers and environmental scientists studying relationships between the physical environment and human activity. The department has particular strengths in geospatial analysis, field methods, and climate and environmental change and is home to undergraduate and graduate programs in geography, environmental and sustainability science, and GIS . Located in Washington, D.C., GW provides exceptional opportunities for collaboration with federal agencies, NGOs, and research institutions. GW is a Carnegie R1 research university. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Procedure: Please complete an online application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129037, uploading the following documents: Cover Letter. A current curriculum vitae (CV). A Statement of research interests. A statement of teaching interests/philosophy. Transcripts of all college work. Unofficial transcripts will suffice for the application. Official transcripts must be submitted immediately upon employment. Email and phone number of three professional references. Reference letters may be requested later. Review of applications will begin November 12, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://geography.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129037 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript Statement of Teaching Interest Statement of Research Interest Names and Contact Information for References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a PhD in Geography, Environmental Science, or a related field by the time of appointment? Yes No * Can you demonstrate research and/or teaching success using field and quantitative or geospatial methods? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128712": {
      "title": "Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. When applying for the Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please visit https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128364 and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002654 Academic Title: Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering Rank: Librarian I, Librarian II, Librarian III, Librarian IV Administrative Title: Discipline Libraries Specialty: Contract Type: Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - Renewable period depending on rank at date of hire. Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Libraries and Academic Innovation ( GWLAI ) enriches the academic experience of scholars and students and sparks innovation at GW. We enable research and teaching through access to the latest scholarship and rich archival resources, tailored support for researchers at all levels, guidance for faculty who want to explore new teaching methods and technologies in the classroom, and robust support for online education. Through innovative partnerships, dynamic workshops, and team-based approaches to project management and problem solving, GWLAI fosters collaboration and provides leadership across the university to support the shared mission of generating, making accessible, and preserving new knowledge. Having joined the Association of American Universities ( AAU ) in 2023, and guided by a new Strategic Framework , GW is at an exciting moment in its history and trajectory, and GWLAI is a key partner in supporting the university’s research and scholarly advancements and promoting discoveries and innovations made by the research community. GWLAI seeks a collaborative and service-oriented Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering to join the Research and User Services ( RUS ) department. RUS is a highly collaborative unit where librarians work together and share responsibility for meeting the full range of student, faculty, and researcher needs across disciplines. This position plays a vital role in supporting interdisciplinary teaching, research, and publishing, with an emphasis on supporting the natural sciences, engineering, and data-intensive research fields. As an active member of the RUS team, the incumbent also provides research support, instruction, and collection development services to all areas of the university, including the First Year Writing program. GWLAI staff and librarians are champions of open access and support open scholarly communication and publishing practices, including the adoption and creation of open educational resources ( OER ). Librarians contribute to the scholarly community through research, professional engagement, and service. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Support the research and instructional needs of faculty, students, and researchers in the sciences, engineering, and related interdisciplinary fields. Conduct library instruction for undergraduate and graduate level courses in partnership with faculty, including partnering with GW’s first-year University Writing Program. Provide research consultations and services (chat, email) across disciplines. Participate in collaborative collection development and relationship-building with departments and research units to understand and meet their evolving needs. Provide expert guidance on scientific research methods and navigating scientific literature, reproducible research workflows, datasets, and data analysis tools. Contribute to workshops, outreach, and programming that advance data literacy, computational fluency, and research transparency. Contribute to strategic initiatives or teams within GWLAI , including efforts related to scholarly communication, open access publishing, open education, research impact and visibility, and/or data literacy and computational fluency. Minimum Qualifications: ALA -accredited Master’s degree in library or information science OR other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment. Demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community. Strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and challenges facing researchers in an academic environment. Experience or demonstrated potential to support scientific research, instruction, and publishing practices within science and engineering fields. Advertised Salary: Librarian 1: $58,566 - $65,000; Librarian 2: $61,156 - $78,000; Librarian 3: $65,156 - $81,000; Librarian 4: $71,656 - $130,000 Other Benefits: Salary and appointment at the rank of Librarian I/II/ III /IV are dependent upon qualifications. Salary is negotiable, contingent upon rank, skills and qualifications and is competitive for DC-area academic libraries. Comprehensive benefits package includes 22 days/year paid annual leave; 12 days/year paid sick leave; paid winter break and 8 other holidays; medical, dental, and vision; 401(A) retirement plan, 4% base and GW will match 150% of the first 4% of your 403(B) contributions, up to a maximum of 6% of your eligible compensation; tuition assistance; ongoing support for professional development; and paid parental leave. Librarians are eligible to apply for research leave after a defined period of service. For benefit details, please visit GW Benefits . This position is classified as a Council of Librarians position and is eligible for a hybrid on-campus/remote work schedule. This position is a continual reappointment position with reappointment periods of 3-5 years depending on rank. Proven commitment to the profession is expected and can be exhibited through service, publication, and/or presentations Other Information: PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Work experience, degree, or coursework in sciences, computer sciences, or other engineering related fields. Experience with data analysis, GIS , coding, visualization, or computational research tools. Familiarity with research data management, open science practices, and reproducible research methods. Experience supporting systematic review projects or teaching about systematic review methodology. We recognize that strong candidates may not meet every qualification. If you are passionate about this role, we encourage you to apply and highlight how your experiences align with the position. This position reports to a Director of Research Services and is eligible for partial telework. The University and GWLAI have a strong commitment to recruiting librarians of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the University with different experiences and perspectives. We offer a work environment that values and supports collaboration, teamwork, and professional growth and development. A virtual information session for interested candidates will be offered in the coming weeks. Please visit https://go.gwu.edu/librarianjobs for details. Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying for the Research Services Librarian for Science and Engineering position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please visit https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128364 and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Department Link: http://library.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128364 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Resume Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an ALA-accredited Master's degree in library or information science or other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community? Yes No * Do you have a strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and challenges facing researchers in an academic environment? Yes No * Do you have experience or demonstrated potential to support scientific research, instruction, and publishing practices within science and engineering fields? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
