    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125239": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologist)",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologist) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologist) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on May 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002605 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Advanced Heart Failure Cardiologist) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Cardiology (Advanced Heart Failure) Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 7/1/2026-6/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent, non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, is seeking a full-time academic advanced heart failure cardiologist to join the growing Heart Failure/Mechanical Circulatory Support section of the Department of Medicine. This non-tenure-track appointment, expected to begin as early as Summer 2026, will be made at a rank (instructor, assistant/associate professor, professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing excellent patient care to hospitalized patients; conducting outpatient consultations, including performing right heart catheterizations and endomyocardial biopsies; teaching residents, fellows, and medical students; and maintaining an active scholarly program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-eligible/board-certified in advanced heart failure and transplantation and licensed in the District of Columbia by the time of appointment. Applicants must have demonstrated skills in the area of advanced heart failure and mechanical circulatory assist devices, including complex heart failure management; pre- and post- VAD management, including other temporary mechanical circulatory support devices; and cardiac intensive care management. Advertised Salary: $287,000 to $400,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on May 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://medicine.smhs.gwu.edu/cardiology Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125194 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-eligible/board-certified in advanced heart failure and transplantation by the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be licensed in the District of Columbia by the time of appointment? Yes No * Do have demonstrated skills in the area of advanced heart failure and mechanical circulatory assist devices, including complex heart failure management? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated skills in pre- and post-VAD management, including other temporary mechanical circulatory support devices? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated skills in the area of cardiac intensive care management? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
