    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118821": {
      "title": "Faculty Position - Molecular Pathology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Position - Molecular Pathology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Position - Molecular Pathology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter describing your qualifications for the position. Review of applications will begin on October 10, 2024, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002415 Academic Title: Faculty Position - Molecular Pathology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/1/2024-6/30/2025 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2024 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) Department of Pathology is recruiting a full-time Molecular Pathologist. The MFA is an independent non-profit faculty clinical practice group affiliated with the George Washington University (GW) School of Medicine and Health Sciences ( SMHS ) and the flagship George Washington University Hospital, located in a vibrant campus in the heart of the nation’s capital. We seek candidates with experience in molecular genetic/genomic testing, including next-generation sequencing for molecular oncology and other molecular assays. Candidates with FISH biomarker testing are welcome to apply as well. Candidates with additional expertise in cytopathology and/or neuropathology will be considered. Opportunities are available for active research as independent investigators or in collaboration with other clinicians and basic investigators. Candidates with strong research backgrounds who may establish principal investigator-led research may also be considered for appropriate research support and laboratory space. This faculty appointment will be in the non-tenure track at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) MD and MD/PhD candidates must be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia. This position is expected to begin as early as December 2024. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include developing, validating, implementing, and reporting molecular test results, regulatory compliance, accreditation, quality management, and training residents, fellows, and students. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess a PhD, MD, or MD/PhD or equivalent degree and be eligible for or board-certified in clinical pathology, anatomic and clinical pathology, molecular genetic pathology, and/or American Board of Medical Genetics and Genomics. They must also have fellowship training in molecular pathology or prior molecular pathologist experience. Advertised Salary: Salary will be commensurate with experience within the $200,000 to $289,000 range. Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter describing your qualifications for the position. Review of applications will begin on October 10, 2024, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://pathology.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/112588 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD, MD, or MD/PhD or equivalent degree? Yes No * Will you be eligible for or board-certified in clinical pathology, anatomic and clinical pathology, molecular genetic pathology, and/or American Board of Medical Genetics and Genomics? Yes No * Do you have fellowship training in molecular pathology or prior molecular pathologist experience? Yes No * If you have an MD or MD/PhD, are you eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129117": {
      "title": "Hospitalist &amp; Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Hospitalist &amp; Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Hospitalist & Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002663 Academic Title: Hospitalist & Consultation-Liaison Psychiatrists Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/01/2026 - 06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University and Capital Medical Group, formerly known as the Medical Faculty Associates, are seeking academic hospitalist psychiatrists for full-time, regular faculty appointments in the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Health. Candidates with fellowship training in consultation-liaison psychiatry are invited to apply. These non-tenure-track positions, expected to start as early as Winter 2026, will be filled at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience, ranging from $280,000 to $320,000. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include serving on the psychiatry hospitalist team, which supports medical-surgery units, the inpatient psychiatric service, and the emergency department; teaching medical students and psychiatry residents; seeing patients in an outpatient setting; and developing a clinical research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in General Psychiatry and license-eligible in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $280,000 to $320,000 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The Capital Medical Group also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://jobs.uhsinc.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Department Link: https://psychiatry.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128905 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated 