    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/121305": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Infectious Diseases",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Position in Infectious Diseases Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Position in Infectious Diseases Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on August 18, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002552 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Position in Infectious Diseases Rank: Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Infectious Diseases Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 9/1/25-6/30/26 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 09/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ), an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University School of Medicine & Health Sciences, is seeking a full-time academic Infectious Disease physician for its Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Medicine. The Division of Infectious Diseases sees a diverse patient population with a broad range of infectious diseases. Its primary research focus has long been HIV / AIDS , with involvement in studies on both HIV prevention as a clinical research site for the HIV Prevention Trials Network, and HIV treatment through multiple industry-sponsored trials. The Division is also heavily involved in vaccine research as part of the Project NextGen COVID -19 Initiative, as well as vaccine research for HIV , RSV , Ebola, Marburg, Influenza, C. difficile, and mpox. This non-tenure-track faculty appointment, expected to start as early as Fall 2025, will be made at a rank (Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The physician will be integrated into all aspects of the Division of Infectious Diseases, including attending on the inpatient consult service at George Washington University Hospital and Cedar Hill Regional Medical Center, staffing the outpatient Infectious Diseases clinic, teaching medical students, residents, and Infectious Diseases fellows, and collaborating in the research programs of the Division. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Infectious Diseases and must be licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $157,500.00 to $210,000.00 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on August 18, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/infectious-diseases Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/119497 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in Infectious Diseases at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
