    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124808": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002563 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Rank: Assistant Professor, Instructor, Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: General Internal Medicine Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/26-06/30/27 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, seeks full-time academic physicians to join our Division of Primary Care in the Department of Medicine. Join a collaborative and mission-driven team of clinician-educators in downtown Washington, DC. These positions offer a unique opportunity to engage in clinical care and medical education. These non-tenure-track faculty appointments, expected to start as early as July 2026, will be made at a rank (Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing direct, high-quality patient care in an outpatient setting; engaging in population health management and quality/safety initiatives; participating in administrative duties; and contributing to the teaching and mentorship of medical students, interns, residents, fellows, and other learners. All faculty are encouraged to develop scholarly interests and are expected to collaborate with the larger team to enhance access, reduce costs, improve quality, and promote better health outcomes. Faculty can receive up to 10% protected time for research in the first year. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be ABIM -certified or eligible and licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Applicants must also have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth. Advertised Salary: $170,000.00 - $220,000.00 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://medicine.smhs.gwu.edu/general-internal-medicine Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120140 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be ABIM-certified or eligible at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120007": {
      "title": "Comprehensive Otolaryngologist",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Comprehensive Otolaryngologist Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Comprehensive Otolaryngologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on June 2, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002513 Academic Title: Comprehensive Otolaryngologist Rank: Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Professor Administrative Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Otolaryngology Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Otolaryngology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 7/1/2025-6/30/2026 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) is seeking a full-time faculty member in the Department of Surgery’s Division of Otolaryngology with a primary interest in comprehensive otolaryngology. The MFA is an independent, non-profit clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University. This non-tenure track position, expected to start as early as Summer 2025, will be made at a rank (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Surgery’s faculty are committed to patient care, cohesive and focused team building, administrative leadership, as well as resident and medical student education. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or board-eligible by the American Board of Otolaryngology, have completed an ACGME -accredited residency in otolaryngology, and be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Applicants must also demonstrate clinical expertise in general otolaryngology, as documented by residency surgical case logs and faculty references. Advertised Salary: $350,000-400,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on June 2, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/119750 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or board-eligible by the American Board of Otolaryngology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you have completed an ACGME-accredited residency in otolaryngology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Can you demonstrate clinical expertise in general otolaryngology, as documented by residency surgical case logs and faculty references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129212": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy &amp; Cell Biology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy &amp; Cell Biology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy & Cell Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV, cover letter, and teaching statement. Review of applications will begin on September 23, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002640 Academic Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Anatomy & Cell Biology Rank: Associate Professor, Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Gross Anatomy and either Histology/Neuroanatomy Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 01/01/2027-06/30/2028 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 01/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Anatomy and Cell Biology at The George Washington University School of Medicine and Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time (12-month) non-tenure-track faculty position at the assistant or associate professor level with a salary commensurate with experience. This position is expected to begin as early as January 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching didactic and laboratory courses in Gross Anatomy and either/Histology/Neuroanatomy. All courses are team-taught with a strong clinical emphasis. Additional responsibilities include engagement in scholarly activities and providing service at the departmental, school, and university levels. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have a terminal degree (PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent) in anatomy or a related field, or must have completed all the requirements for their doctoral degree by the date of appointment. Experience in teaching at the university level is required. Advertised Salary: $125,000 to $180,000 Other Benefits: The George Washington University provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV, cover letter, and teaching statement. Review of applications will begin on September 23, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127478 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a terminal degree (PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent) in anatomy or a related field, or have completed all the requirements for your doctoral degree by the date of appointment Yes No * Do you have experience teaching at the university level? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
