    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120315": {
      "title": "Vice Chair for Research - Neurology and Rehabilitation Medicine",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Vice Chair for Research - Neurology and Rehabilitation Medicine Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Vice Chair for Research - Neurology and Rehabilitation Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, applicants should complete an online faculty application and upload a letter of interest, a CV, and the contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin June 20, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002511 Academic Title: Vice Chair for Research - Neurology and Rehabilitation Medicine Rank: Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Vice Chair for Research Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 9/1/25-6/30/26 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 09/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington Medical Faculty Associates’ Department of Neurology and Rehabilitation medicine is seeking a physician or non-physician scientist for the position of Vice Chair of Research. The sought Vice Chair for Research is a visionary and dynamic leader. This senior leadership role is critical to advancing our mission to become a nationally recognized center of excellence in neurological research. The Vice Chair for Research will shape the department’s research trajectory, mentor the next generation of clinician-scientists, and foster collaborative, interdisciplinary initiatives.The appointment, expected to begin as early as Fall 2025, will be at the rank of associate or full professor, and a competitive start-up package will be provided to support the successful candidate’s research program. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The Vice Chair for Research will play a pivotal role in positioning the Department of Neurology as a leader in innovative research, ultimately transforming care for patients with neurological disorders, and will share our ambition and are ready to lead with creativity, passion, and vision. The Vice Chair of Research’s responsibilities will include: conducting independent research aligned with the department’s academic vision, securing extramural funding from federal, industry, and philanthropic sources, establishing new research initiatives with a focus on translational and clinical science, providing mentorship and faculty development through structured programs, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration with basic science and clinical departments, overseeing research operations including resource management and regulatory compliance, advocating for the department’s research mission, and engaging with the community and philanthropic partners to support research initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be an MD, PhD, or MD/PhD with a distinguished research record in a relevant field of neurology and demonstrated success in securing extramural funding and leading research teams. Applicants must have a strong track record of mentorship and faculty development and display excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to inspire and unite diverse stakeholders. Applicants must also commit to fostering an inclusive and equitable research environment. Advertised Salary: $175,000 to $350,000. Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, applicants should complete an online faculty application and upload a letter of interest, a CV, and the contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin June 20, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/neurology/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/119494 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an MD, PhD, or MD/PhD? Yes No * Do you have a distinguished research record in a relevant field of neurology? Yes No * Can you demonstrate success in securing extramural funding and leading research teams? Yes No * Do you have a strong track record of mentorship and faculty development? Yes No * Can you display excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to inspire and unite diverse stakeholders? Yes No * Do you display excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to inspire and unite diverse stakeholders? Yes No * Will you commit to fostering an inclusive and equitable research environment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
