    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129233": {
      "title": "Senior Member Service Coordinator",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Member Service Coordinator Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Member Service Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The Division for Student Affairs cultivates an inclusive community that supports connection, growth, and well-being for every student throughout their GW journey. DSA’s integrated approach is to provide a cohesive student experience built upon the core values of genuine collaboration, a compassionate approach, and most importantly, putting students at the center of the work. Campus Recreation, within the Division for Student Affairs, strives to create a space and environment for students to move joyfully, explore different types of physical activity, enjoy constructive competitive opportunities for individuals of all abilities and connect with others in meaningful ways. The home base for programming is the Lerner Health and Wellness Center ( LHWC ). Campus Recreation offers a diverse range of programming opportunities, including intramural sports, club sports, group fitness classes, personal training sessions, fitness clinics and workshops, outdoor education programs, drop-in recreation, and certification courses. This Senior Member Service Coordinator position will report to the Student Development Manager for Campus Recreation and is responsible for: Coordinate and monitor all membership sales, locker rentals, and front desk access control. Identify and pursue opportunities that will improve revenue generation, service quality and operational effectiveness for the facility and its services. Work closely with the Associate Director to review financial reconciliations related revenue collection including memberships, programs and services for Campus Recreation. Manage all aspects of the business operations software system which encompasses a membership CRM , access control, activity registration, equipment rental, online purchasing and payment processing modules. Liaison for GW IT, GWorld and all external groups. Implement a comprehensive marketing plan designed to maximize membership and revenue, while also expanding guest participation and engagement. Lead the development, production, and distribution of physical and digital promotions and external email communications. Coordinate coverage and represent Campus Recreation at various events throughout the year. Develop and delivers training and establishes guidelines for student staff development in the areas of membership sales and guest services. Supervise and evaluate up to 15 Fitness Attendants, 25 Guest Service Attendants, and 1 Marketing Assistant. The position is based at GW’s Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington, DC. The incumbent may be assigned other related duties as needed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Obtained within the first 90 days: CPR / AED /First Aid from American Red Cross or equivalent DC Certified Pool Operator Preferred Qualifications: General knowledge of office management techniques. Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, the Internet, E-mail) and in using standard office equipment. Ability to demonstrate effective communication skills both orally and in writing. Ability to analyze and interpret policy and procedural questions. Ability to research and resolve office management problems and questions. Ability to organize workflow and coordinate activities. Ability to prioritize workload. Ability to update skills on a continual basis. Hiring Range $44,985.20 - $57,788.56 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Student Affairs Family Student Affairs Sub-Family Campus Recreation Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday – Friday 8:30am - 4:30pm with occasional evening or weekend work for Campus Recreation or DSA events Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Telework: No Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014511 Job Open Date: 10/08/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)? (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently possess the following certifications? CPR/AED/First Aid certification from the American Red Cross or an equivalent provider DC Certified Pool Operator (CPO) certification Both None * If you do not currently possess one or both of the certifications listed above, are you willing and able to obtain any missing certification(s) within ninety (90) days of employment? Yes No * Do you understand and acknowledge that, if hired, you must obtain any missing certification(s) within ninety (90) days of employment? Yes No Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128501": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (3) a current CV, (4) one or at most two research papers, (5) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (6) teaching evaluations (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002647 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Economics and International Affairs Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University’s Elliott School of International Affairs and Department of Economics invite applications for two full-time, tenure-track faculty positions beginning Fall 2027. We seek applicants specializing in international trade. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities will include courses for undergraduate and graduate students in the Elliott School and the Economics Department, and the candidate should maintain flexibility regarding the eventual teaching portfolio. The position will be affiliated with the Elliott School’s Institute for International Economic Policy and Master’s programs in International Economic Policy, International Development Studies, and International Science and Technology Policy. Elliott School faculty maintain engagement with policy issues and the policy community as a general criterion for appointment. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in economics with a primary focus on international trade. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or complete all requirements for the Ph.D. by the date of appointment. Applications at the mid-level or senior assistant professor level will also be strongly considered. Advertised Salary: $150,000-$165,000 Other Benefits: GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (3) a current CV, (4) one or at most two research papers, (5) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (6) teaching evaluations (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128100 Applicant Documents Required Documents Statement of Teaching and Research Interest Curriculum Vitae Other Documents Refer to Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter Optional Documents Course Evaluations or Summaries Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
