    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128674": {
      "title": "Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. When applying for the Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002653 Academic Title: Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Rank: Librarian I, Librarian II, Librarian III, Librarian IV Administrative Title: Discipline Libraries Specialty: Contract Type: Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - Renewable period depending on rank at date of hire. Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 10/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Libraries and Academic Innovation ( GWLAI ) enriches the academic experience of scholars and students and sparks innovation at GW. We enable research and teaching through access to the latest scholarship and rich archival resources, tailored support for researchers at all levels, guidance for faculty who want to explore new teaching methods and technologies in the classroom, and robust support for online education. Through innovative partnerships, dynamic workshops, and team-based approaches to project management and problem solving, GWLAI fosters collaboration and provides leadership across the university to support the shared mission of generating, making accessible, and preserving new knowledge. Having joined the Association of American Universities ( AAU ) in 2023, and guided by a new Strategic Framework , GW is at an exciting moment in its history and trajectory, and GWLAI is a key partner in supporting the university’s research and scholarly advancements and promoting discoveries and innovations made by the research community. GWLAI seeks a collaborative and service-oriented Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences to join the Research and User Services ( RUS ) department. RUS is a highly collaborative unit where librarians work together and share responsibility for meeting the full range of student, faculty, and researcher needs across disciplines. This position plays a vital role in supporting interdisciplinary teaching, research, and publishing across the Social and Political Sciences with an emphasis on international affairs, political science, public policy, economics, and related fields. As an active member of the RUS team, the incumbent also provides research support, instruction, and collection development services to all areas of the university, including the First Year Writing program. GWLAI staff and librarians are champions of open access and support open scholarly communication and publishing practices, including the adoption and creation of open educational resources ( OER ). Librarians contribute to the scholarly community through research, professional engagement, and service. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Support the research and instructional needs of faculty, students, and researchers in the Social and Political Sciences, with an emphasis on international affairs, political science, public policy, economics, and related fields. Conduct library instruction for undergraduate and graduate level courses in partnership with faculty, including partnering with GW’s first-year University Writing Program. Provide research consultations and services (chat, email) across disciplines. Participate in collaborative collection development and relationship-building with departments and research units to understand and meet their evolving needs. Provide expert guidance on Social Science research methods, statistical data analysis, visualization and use, text and data mining, and/or other quantitative and qualitative research methods. Contribute to strategic initiatives or teams within GWLAI , including efforts related to scholarly communication, open access publishing, open education, research impact and visibility, and/or data literacy and computational fluency. Minimum Qualifications: ALA -accredited Master’s degree in library and information science OR other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment. Demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community. Strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles Excellent oral and written communication skills. Awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and challenges facing researchers in an academic environment. Experience or demonstrated potential to support Social Science research methods and publishing practices. Advertised Salary: Librarian 1: $58,566 - $65,000; Librarian 2: $61,156 - $78,000; Librarian 3: $65,156 - $81,000; Librarian 4: $71,656 - $130,000 Other Benefits: Salary and appointment at the rank of Librarian I/II/ III /IV are dependent upon qualifications. Salary is negotiable, contingent upon rank, skills and qualifications and is competitive for DC area academic libraries. Comprehensive benefits package includes 22 days/year paid annual leave; 12 days/year paid sick leave; paid winter break and 8 other holidays; medical, dental, and vision; 401(A) retirement plan, 4% base and GW will match 150% of the first 4% of your 403(B) contributions, up to a maximum of 6% of your eligible compensation; tuition assistance; ongoing support for professional development; and paid parental leave. Librarians are eligible to apply for research leave after a defined period of service. For benefit details, please visit GW Benefits . This position is classified as a Council of Librarians position and is eligible for a hybrid on-campus/remote work schedule. This position is a continual reappointment position with reappointment periods of 3-5 years depending on rank. Proven commitment to the profession is expected and can be exhibited through service, publication, and/or presentations. Other Information: PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of, or experience working with, financial and economic data. A strong understanding of the research lifecycle, scholarly communication, and academic publishing. A robust understanding of computational and data research methods, statistical data analysis and use methods, text and data mining, or other quantitative and qualitative research methods. Experience with GIS , coding, data visualization, or computational research tools. We recognize that strong candidates may not meet every qualification. If you are passionate about this role, we encourage you to apply and highlight how your experiences align with the position. This position reports to a Director of Research Services and is eligible for partial telework. The University and GWLAI have a strong commitment to recruiting librarians of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the University with different experiences and perspectives. We offer a work environment that values and supports collaboration, teamwork, and professional growth and development. A virtual information session for interested candidates will be offered in the coming weeks. Please visit https://go.gwu.edu/librarianjobs for details. Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying for the Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Department Link: http://library.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128316 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Resume Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an ALA-accredited Master’s degree in library and information science OR other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community? Yes No * Do you have a strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and challenges facing researchers in an academic environment? Yes No * Do you have experience or demonstrated potential to support Social Science research methods and publishing practices? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125052": {
      "title": "Professor or Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Professor or Associate Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Professor or Associate Professor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on June 26, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002426 Academic Title: Professor or Associate Professor of Nursing Rank: Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Executive Associate Dean Discipline Nursing Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 10/01/2025 - 06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Executive Associate Dean serves as the Chief Operating Officer and is responsible for the operational functions that enable the execution of the strategic plan and achievement of the school’s goals and mission. The Executive Associate Dean is a member of the Dean’s senior leadership team and is responsible for the operational efficiency and effectiveness of the organization by being responsible for the development, design, operation, and improvement of the systems that will lead to the full execution of the strategic plan. Collaboration with all members of the SON’s leadership is an integral part of this role. The Executive Associate Dean may act on behalf of the Dean as delegated. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenured faculty at the Associate or Professor rank, with a start date as early as July 2025. We welcome applicants with advanced practice certification. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: · Serves as a direct liaison between the academic and administrative functions of the SON by identifying the resources required for implementation of the strategic plan and potential obstacles that need to be addressed. · Cascades the school’s mission statement throughout the school for maximal alignment and develops appropriate recognition and coaching practices to align personnel with school goals. · Drives performance measures for the operation of the strategic plan, often in the form of dashboards convenient for review of high-level key indicators. Ensures SON policies and practices are established and implemented and are compliant with all applicable laws, regulations, and University policies and procedures. · Facilitates the operational activities of the Associate Deans for Prelicense/Baccalaureate programs, Graduate Clinical programs, PhD program, and the Associate Deans for Practice and Community Engagement, Research and Health Policy & Population Science. · In collaboration with the Senior Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs, Finance manager and HR partners works with unit leaders in the management of resources, as well as the development and execution of unit budgets. · Collaborates with other SON leaders on pertinent issues and activities that span the tripartite mission. · Participate with other campus academic officers in the development of university- wide academic priorities and goals and in the implementation of inter-disciplinary programs to achieve defined ends; serves on committees and councils of the School, the University and other agencies and organizations. Minimum Qualifications: · An earned doctoral degree in nursing or a health-related field · Prior academic administrative experience with evidence of increasing administrative responsibility · Prior organizational and/or program planning experience · Prior experiences with organizational strategic planning and implementation · At least five years of teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level · Experience with curriculum development and revision · Experience with accreditation self-study and preparation of reports for boards of Nursing, accreditors, and regulatory agencies. · Evidence of ability to advance diversity, equity and inclusion efforts through teaching, research/scholarship and/or service · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills · Eligibility for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia. Advertised Salary: $175,000 to $225,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on June 26, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/113464 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctoral degree in nursing or a health-related field? Yes No * Do you have prior academic administrative experience with evidence of increasing administrative responsibility? Yes No * Do you have prior organizational and/or program planning experience? Yes No * Do you have prior experience with organizational strategic planning and implementation? Yes No * Do you have at least five years of teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level? Yes No * Do you have experience with curriculum development and revision? Yes No * Do you have experience with accreditation self-study and preparation of reports for boards of Nursing, accreditors, and regulatory agencies? Yes No * Can you demonstrate evidence of ability to advance diversity, equity and inclusion efforts through teaching, research/scholarship and/or service? Yes No * Do you have excellent interpersonal and communication skills? Yes No * Are you eligible for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129517": {
      "title": "Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: GW’s School of Nursing (GW Nursing) drives innovation and improvements in healthcare worldwide through the education of compassionate nurses, esteemed educators and researchers, entrepreneurial leaders, and influential policy experts. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement is responsible for coordination of clinical and field experience placements of students enrolled in the Post-Master’s Certificate ( PMC ), MSN , and DNP programs. This role serves as the liaison between School of Nursing ( SON ), GW SON students, and clinical partners, and maintains a strong relationship with the local healthcare community. The incumbent will initiate, negotiate and review contracts for execution between the university and our clinical affiliates, support students in their searches and tracking their compliance items. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement position requires strong interpersonal skills, attention to detail, critical thinking, and be able to work autonomously. This position will report to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement position will collaborate with Clinical Placement team members in the assignment of clinical sites, as well as provide support for students needing clinical or field placements. The Program Associate, Graduate Clinical Placement will process requests, communicate requirements and steps to students, assist with data collection, maintain relationships with faculty, and present clinical placement policies and procedures to ensure that clinical placements are processed and obtained. Responsibilities include: Works independently to process clinical and field experience requests for PMC , MSN , & DNP students. Cultivates and sustains good relationships with preceptors and sites and maintains preceptor and clinical site databases. Coordinates and performs record keeping and correspondence related to clinical/practicum experiences for all graduate nursing students. Organizes and participates in orientation sessions and other educational workshops. Works in collaboration with the program leadership to ensure program-specific information is communicated with students. Responsible for initiating, negotiating and executing affiliation agreements/contracts between GW SON and external clinical site/partners to ensure compliance with university regulations. Monitors student compliance through compliance tracking system. Coordinates clinical activities, create clinical reports tracking student clinical experiences in the clinical management program as required for accreditation. Assists with data collection, sets up data sets, and provides periodic data analysis to identify opportunities for process and outcome improvements. Develops and facilitates effective working relationships and communication as well as providing quality service with both internal and external constituents, clinical sites/preceptors. Effectively utilizes the clinical management system/program to manage all aspects of the clinical placement process, including but not limited to student placements, evaluation, documentation, and reporting as needed to meet CCNE and program standards. Develops and maintains tracking systems and databases to ensure the efficient and effective management of administrative and clinical activities, and provides proactive reporting analysis to leadership and clinical curriculum committee. Participates in the CCNE accreditation meetings and on-site evaluation. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Ashburn, Virginia College/School/Department: School of Nursing Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 40 Hiring Range $18.40 - $28.81 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T001337 Job Open Date: Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: No Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is your expected hourly range? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129017": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: (1) a cover letter; (2) an updated CV; (3) a statement of teaching and research interests (1-3 pages); (4) two samples of scholarly publications; and (5) two recent course evaluation summaries. Address cover letter to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, George Washington University School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on September 10, 2026 and will continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002634 Academic Title: Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Open Rank Administrative Title: Discipline Nursing Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 09/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington School of Nursing invites qualified applicants for a tenure-track open rank faculty position. The School’s research interests include symptom science, oncology, behavioral health, health policy and population health. This full-time, 12-month position is scheduled to begin as early as fall 2026. This is an on-campus position, not remote. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: · Develop and maintain an independent, externally funded research program · Maintain an ongoing record of scholarly productivity, including publications and presentations · Teach courses as assigned · Mentor and advise students in research · Participate in collaborative, interdisciplinary research teams · Participate in faculty governance, including serving on departmental, school, and/or university committees · and participate in a professional capacity in nursing and research organizations at the national and international level. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Earned PhD in nursing, public health, education or related field by the date of application 2. A nursing degree at any level 3. An emerging body of scholarship, as evidenced by presentations and peer-reviewed publications 4. Track record of external funding 5. Strong methodological and statistical skills 6. Prior college-level teaching experience is required, including comfort with in-person and online learning 7. Eligibility for unencumbered DC and VA nursing licensure Advertised Salary: $120,000 to $200,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits Other Information: All faculty hiring decisions will be contingent upon final approval by the Provost. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: (1) a cover letter; (2) an updated CV; (3) a statement of teaching and research interests (1-3 pages); (4) two samples of scholarly publications; and (5) two recent course evaluation summaries. Address cover letter to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, George Washington University School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on September 10, 2026 and will continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/126837 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Sample Publications Statement of Teaching and Research Interest Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an earned PhD in nursing, public health, education or related field by date of application? Yes No * Do you have a nursing degree (any level)? Yes No * Do you have an emerging body of scholarship as evidenced by presentations and peer-reviewed publications? Yes No * Do you have a track record of external funding? Yes No * Do you have strong methodological and statistical skills? Yes No * Do you have prior college-level teaching experience, including comfort with in-person and online learning? Yes No * Are you eligible for unencumbered nursing license in DC and VA? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128718": {
      "title": "Director of Development, GWSB",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Director of Development, GWSB Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Director of Development, GWSB Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The George Washington University Advancement Division seeks a Director of Development for the GW School of Business ( GWSB ). Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Development, this position serves as a lead fundraiser for the School and plays a key role in advancing the University’s mission through the cultivation of philanthropic support. The Director serves as the primary relationship manager for a portfolio of major and principal gift prospects, developing authentic and enduring partnerships with alumni, parents, friends, and other constituents that lead to transformational philanthropic support for the GW School of Business and the university. The Director manages a portfolio of approximately 120 major gift prospects and donors, developing and executing strategies for identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship. Through meaningful engagement and donor-centered relationship building, the Director aligns philanthropic interests with institutional priorities and secures gifts of $50,000 and above, including gifts exceeding $1million. The Director partners with the Assistant Vice President, Dean, faculty, and Advancement colleagues to execute fundraising strategies and advance philanthropic priorities for the School of Business and the university. Working collaboratively across Advancement, the Director helps strengthen donor engagement, expand philanthropic support, and advance strategic initiatives that support student success, faculty excellence, academic programs, research, and capital priorities. Primary Responsibilities: Manage and advance a portfolio of approximately 120 major and principal gift prospects and donors. Build and sustain meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, friends, and other key constituents to deepen engagement and inspire philanthropic investment in the School and university. Develop and execute individualized donor strategies that move prospects through the donor lifecycle, from identification and qualification through solicitation and stewardship. Secure major, principal and planned gifts in support of institutional priorities. Conduct approximately 15 prospect visits per month and maintain a high level of meaningful donor engagement activity. Partner with leadership to align fundraising efforts with institutional priorities. Prepare prospect strategy materials and briefing documents for university leadership. Collaborate closely with Advancement partners to identify, qualify, and cultivate high-capacity prospects. Support campaign planning and other strategic fundraising initiatives for the School and university. Handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Participate in Advancement-wide initiatives, committees, and working groups that strengthen fundraising effectiveness and donor engagement. The successful candidate will demonstrate a proven record of securing major and principal gifts through effective donor identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship. The Director will serve as a strategic fundraising partner within Advancement and contribute to team-wide overarching goals, initiatives and best practices. This position requires significant local and national travel with the possibility of international travel, along with the flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning responsibilities that are reasonably related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 6 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree in a relevant area of study plus 4 years of relevant experience. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to achieve results independently while collaborating effectively with colleagues to advance shared fundraising goals. Ability to build strong relationships with donors, volunteers, faculty, administrators, and other stakeholders. Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills. Strong organizational, project management, and database management skills, with exceptional attention to detail. Sound judgment and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential information. Ability to work effectively with diverse constituencies and engage volunteer leaders. Creative, resourceful, and persistent approach to achieving fundraising objectives. Proven success meeting or exceeding fundraising goals, including prospect activity, donor visits, proposals and philanthropic revenue. Ability and willingness to travel regularly and work occasional evenings and weekends. Hiring Range $123,884.24 - $173,365.68 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: University Advancement Family Dev & Alumni Relations Sub-Family Major Gifts Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 4 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm; some evenings and weekends Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014460 Job Open Date: 09/11/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current employee of The George Washington University? Yes No * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)? (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
