    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129297": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Glaucoma)",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Glaucoma) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Glaucoma) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002672 Academic Title: Faculty Positions — Ophthalmology (Glaucoma) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 12/01/2026 - 06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 12/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University and Capital Medical Group, formerly known as the Medical Faculty Associates, are seeking to fill full-time faculty positions in Glaucoma. The positions offer a rare blend of high-quality clinical practice, advanced glaucoma surgery, and hands-on education for medical students and residents. Candidates will have the opportunity to develop a high-volume practice to manage complex glaucoma and cataract, perform cutting-edge procedures, and contribute to training the next generation of ophthalmologists within a collaborative, well-supported environment. The Department of Ophthalmology is part of a growing academic health center located in the heart of a vibrant, world-class metropolitan area with cultural, family, and educational opportunities. These non-tenure-track positions, expected to start as early as Winter 2026, will be filled at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing comprehensive glaucoma laser and incisional procedures and cataract surgeries to a diverse patient population; providing education to the medical students and ophthalmology residents through didactics and clinical and surgical encounters; and contributing to the coverage of the GW Hospital Emergency Department. This call is shared with the other members and paid per night. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Ophthalmology, fellowship-trained in Glaucoma, and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia by the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $300,000 - $400,000 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The Capital Medical Group also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://jobs.uhsinc.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, upload a cover letter and CV, as well as contact information for three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Department Link: https://ophthalmology.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128988 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified or board eligible in Ophthalmology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be fellowship-trained in glaucoma by the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia by time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125682": {
      "title": "Administrative Associate, Temporary",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Administrative Associate, Temporary Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Associate, Temporary Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: GW Temps s is GW’s in-house temporary staffing service. Our temporary staff are assigned throughout the GW campuses in a variety of roles. Temporary assignments can range from one day to many months and can be part-time or full-time. Administrative GW Temps support offices, staff, and executives by performing a variety of tasks that may include answering phones, drafting memos, proof reading, preparing reports, scheduling meetings, ordering supplies, tracking expenses, arranging travel, coordinating events, updating social media accounts, program and project management, interacting with students, faculty, and staff, and fulfilling special assignments and projects. We have temporary assignments as administrative assistants, executive assistants, operation managers, receptionists, data entry assistants, event coordinators, program assistants, and other administrative and operation roles. These positions are on site, five days a week. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED , or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. The degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Detail Oriented Experience in a fast paced envrionment preferred Scheduling experience Zoom experience preferred II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Human Resource Management and Development (HRM&D) Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 40 Hiring Range $26.50 - $34.37 Work Schedule: M-F Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T001155 Job Open Date: 05/04/2026 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
