    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129547": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Research Assistant Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: The Department of Epidemiology is looking to hire a full-time Research Assistant for a research study funded by the National Institutes of Health. The study will be conducted in the GWU Hospital Emergency Department. The primary responsibilities of the job will be: (1) acting as a pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) navigator and resource to the other research assistants (RAs) who work in the emergency department (ED); (2) working in the ED screening and identifying eligible participants, explaining study procedures and obtaining consent, conducting HIV prevention and PrEP medication counseling, providing patients with a PrEP Decision Support Tool and reviewing results with patients, helping to coordinate receipt of PrEP medication including making appointments for patients with community PrEP providers, and providing referrals to social services; and (3) conducting follow-up interviews with participants. It is expected that the candidate selected for this job will develop in-depth knowledge about PrEP and will be comfortable talking to patients, other research staff, and clinical staff about PrEP. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following: Interact with patients and clinical providers to screen, recruit, and consent participants, conduct surveys, collect data, and enter data into a computer. Work with the study coordinator to ensure that the baseline and telephone follow-up interviews are conducted in a timely manner and as successfully as possible. Conduct telephone follow-up with participants Provide daily research support for the assigned research project and related activities, including informed consent, enrollment, data collection (i.e., conducting interviews), data entry, management, and review. Interact with the clinical staff and ensure that study procedures do not disrupt clinical operations where patients are being treated Attend mandatory study team meetings as scheduled and lead the review of enrollment and follow-up results. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a BA/BS in a related discipline. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Employees are required to complete CITI and HIPAA certification if hired. Employees will also be required to complete a PrEP Navigator training program if hired. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience working with HIV and other community-based organizations and populations at risk for HIV is preferred. Strong interest in research and enthusiasm for interacting with people. Strong Communication & Teamwork: Ability to communicate effectively and collaborate seamlessly with project staff, research team members, and emergency department clinical staff. Independent & Detail-Oriented: Capable of managing tasks independently with high accuracy and attention to detail. Computer literacy with Microsoft Word is desired. Hiring Range $18.40 - $27.68 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Milken Institute School of Public Health (SPH) Family Research and Labs Sub-Family Field Research Stream Service and Support Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Telework: Required Background Check Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: R002454 Job Open Date: 10/27/2026 Job Close Date: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)? (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit 