    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/121744": {
      "title": "Faculty Position - Palliative Medicine",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Position - Palliative Medicine Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Position - Palliative Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on September 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002557 Academic Title: Faculty Position - Palliative Medicine Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Palliative Medicine Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 11/1/2025-06/30/2026 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 11/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ), an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University School of Medicine & Health Sciences, seeks a full-time, academic Palliative Medicine physician for its Division of Geriatrics and Palliative Medicine within the Department of Medicine. Persons with specific interest in leadership in inpatient palliative medicine are encouraged to apply. This non-tenure-track faculty appointment, expected to start as early as Fall 2025, will be made at a rank (Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking a physician to join our clinical and education-focused practice, which also supports research. Leadership opportunities exist for competitive candidates, and numerous educational opportunities are available in undergraduate and graduate medical education. The physician will join a well-established consultation service, provide clinical supervision to learners at all levels, serve as faculty for an Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education ( ACGME )-accredited Hospice and Palliative Medicine fellowship program, enjoy teaching opportunities throughout the medical system, and maintain an active research program. Our practice includes a robust inpatient palliative medicine consult service serving a tertiary care hospital and community-based inpatient hospice unit. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Hospice and Palliative Medicine and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Applicants must also have a record of experience and a demonstrated strong interest in training medical students and graduate medical education learners in palliative medicine. Advertised Salary: $190,000 to $210,000 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available, including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on September 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/geriatrics-palliative-medicine Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/121373 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in Hospice and Palliative Medicine at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have a record of experience and a demonstrated strong interest in training medical students and graduate medical education learners in palliative medicine? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129356": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of German Language",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Teaching Assistant Professor of German Language Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Teaching Assistant Professor of German Language Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete an online application and upload the following, clearly addressing the position requirements: 1. a current CV; 2. cover letter outlining how your background and experiences specifically match the qualifications; 3. a statement of teaching philosophy, including your vision for the future success of a German Studies program. Three letters of recommendation with complete titles and contact information for each reference should be sent by the referee to rgss@gwu.edu with the subject line “German Teaching Assistant Professor: [your name]”. (With the exception of the three letters, all other components of an application must be submitted via the gwu.jobs website.) Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002675 Academic Title: Teaching Assistant Professor of German Language Rank: Teaching Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Humanities Specialty: Contract Type: Special Service, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 08/01/27-05/31/30, Non-Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Romance, German, and Slavic Studies at The George Washington University invites applications for one full-time renewable, non-tenure accruing, specialized appointment at the rank of Teaching Assistant Professor of German language to begin as early as fall 2027 with an initial three-year appointment. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Will include but are not limited to teaching seven courses per year in German language and culture; and collaborating on the development, implementation, and assessment of the curriculum. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have a Ph.D. or E.D. in German Studies or related field (area of specialization: open); at least three years’ experience teaching at the college level; native or near-native proficiency in both German and English; demonstrated teaching excellence across different levels and courses in German, as evidenced by evaluations, teaching assessments, letters of recommendation, etc. Advertised Salary: $75,000-80,000 Other Benefits: The successful candidate will be eligible for GW’s benefits programs including medical insurance. Available benefits can be reviewed at https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs Other Information: German at GW is a vibrant undergraduate program within a multilingual department of faculty engaged in dynamic and interdisciplinary teaching and research in languages and cultures. Located in the heart of the nation’s capital, the department is enriched through partnerships with numerous local cultural institutions and embassies. We support community-engaged learning opportunities at all levels of language instruction and partner with units across the university to offer a comprehensive and immersive learning environment for our students. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete an online application and upload the following, clearly addressing the position requirements: 1. a current CV; 2. cover letter outlining how your background and experiences specifically match the qualifications; 3. a statement of teaching philosophy, including your vision for the future success of a German Studies program. Three letters of recommendation with complete titles and contact information for each reference should be sent by the referee to rgss@gwu.edu with the subject line “German Teaching Assistant Professor: [your name]”. (With the exception of the three letters, all other components of an application must be submitted via the gwu.jobs website.) Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://rgss.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129172 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Optional Documents Names and Contact Information for References Course Evaluations or Summaries Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have Ph.D. or E.D. in German Studies or related field Yes No * Do you have at least three years’ experience teaching at the college level? Yes No * Do you have native or near-native proficiency in both German and English? Yes No * Can you demonstrate teaching excellence across different levels and courses in German, as evidenced by evaluations, teaching assessments, letters of recommendation, etc? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129163": {
      "title": "Dedicated Simulation Educator",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Dedicated Simulation Educator Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Dedicated Simulation Educator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The GW Nursing Simulation and Innovation Learning Center is a 20,000 sq. ft. state of the art simulation center on the Virginia Science and Technology Campus. The simulation center was designed by simulation theorist Dr. Pamela Jeffries. At GW Nursing, you are a part of a thriving community of nurse leaders, immersed in simulation pedagogy and dedicated to nursing education excellence. GW Nursing is a catalyst for excellence in nursing education at every degree level, for veterans transitioning to the health care workforce, for groundbreaking research, and for students learning to affect change through health policy and leadership. When it comes to nursing, great work starts with GW! The Dedicated Simulation Educator is responsible for facilitation of nursing simulation-based education scenarios for prelicensure and graduate nursing education. This position is responsible for day to day facilitation, prebriefing, implementing simulation scenarios, and debriefing. Additionally, this role is responsible for ensuring the Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice are maintained, providing evaluation of peers, and evaluation data collection for accreditation. In collaboration with Director of Simulation and Experiential Learning, this role will assist in designing and revising simulation scenarios and will coordinate simulation courses. Additional simulation education activities may include professional development activities around simulation pedagogy, the Healthcare Simulation Standards of Best Practice, policy and procedure updates, and simulation accreditation. This position will also assist with set-up and cleanup of lab space. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Master’s degree in nursing plus 3 years of relevant professional experience, of which at least 2 years must be nursing experience. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: CHSE certification required within two years, CHSE / CHSE -A certification preferred. Must have a VA single or multi-state RN license and is able to practice nursing in VA. Frequent walking and light lifting. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in nursing simulation. Ability to articulate the vision, mission and strategic priorities of the School of Nursing to a variety of audiences. One-year experience in nursing simulation education. Hiring Range $82,950.66 - $114,012.01 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Ashburn, Virginia College/School/Department: School of Nursing Family Academic Affairs Sub-Family Simulation Program Administration Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 3 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday through Friday 8-4:30 with some evenings, rare weekends Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Telework: No Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014501 Job Open Date: 10/05/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * Do you have a VA single or multi-state RN license and are able to practice nursing in VA? Yes No * Please explain your main nursing care specialty. (Open Ended Question) * Please explain your previous experience with simulation education in healthcare. (Open Ended Question) * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/126128": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload the following documents: (1) a cover letter; (2) an updated CV; (3) a statement of teaching interests (1-3 pages); (4) three recent course evaluation summaries; and Address cover letter to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, George Washington University School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin June 29, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. All faculty hiring decisions will be contingent upon final approval by the Provost. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002613 Academic Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Rank: Associate Professor, Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Nursing Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/2026-06/30/2029 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington School of Nursing seeks qualified applicants for an Assistant or Associate Professor position to teach onsite at either our Virginia or Foggy Bottom Campus. This full-time, 9 or 12-month non-tenured faculty position is scheduled to begin as early as Summer 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: · Teaching didactic lectures, clinical courses, and labs as needed in the areas of health assessment, med-surg, critical care/acute care, pharmacology, and pathophysiology · Mentoring students · Providing clinical supervision · Developing curriculum · Maintain an ongoing record of scholarly productivity, including publications and presentations · Participating in faculty governance, including serving on departmental, school, and/or university committees Minimum Qualifications: 1. Doctorate in nursing, education or public health by date of appointment 2. A minimum of 1-2 years of experience teaching in a nursing program 3. Experience with simulation-based learning 4. Evidence of relevant clinical experience 5. Eligibility for unencumbered nursing licensure in DC and VA. Advertised Salary: $120,000 - $150,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload the following documents: (1) a cover letter; (2) an updated CV; (3) a statement of teaching interests (1-3 pages); (4) three recent course evaluation summaries; and Address cover letter to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, George Washington University School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin June 29, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. All faculty hiring decisions will be contingent upon final approval by the Provost. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125533 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a doctorate in nursing, education, public health or related field by the date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of 1-2 years of experience teaching in a nursing program? Yes No * Do you have experience with simulation based learning? Yes No * Can you provide evidence of relevant clinical experience? Yes No * Are you eligible for unencumbered nursing license in DC and VA? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
