    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124136": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Trauma and Acute Care Surgery",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Position in Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Position in Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and a cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on March 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002580 Academic Title: Faculty Position in Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 05/01/2026-6/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 05/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington Medical Faculty Associates’ Department of Surgery seeks a full-time faculty member for the Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Section. The MFA is an independent not-for-profit clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University. This is a non-tenure-track appointment at a rank (instructor, assistant, associate, or full professor) and total compensation, commensurate with experience, ranging from $350,000 to $400,000. This position is expected to begin as early as May 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Our practice is centered in the Washington, DC metropolitan area. We are seeking to recruit a trauma/acute care surgeon with responsibilities to provide trauma, emergency general surgery, and ICU coverage primarily at the George Washington University Level 1 Trauma Center, with the position also involving coverage at our new hospital, Cedar Hill Regional Medical Center. Other responsibilities include teaching fellows, residents, and medical students, as well as contributing to an active research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-eligible or board-certified in general surgery and surgical critical care at the time of appointment. They should have demonstrated excellence in teaching, as evidenced by teaching evaluations; in research, as evidenced by scholarly publications or works in progress; and in clinical care, as evidenced by experience, fellowships, and references. Applicants must also be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia. Advertised Salary: $350,000-400,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and a cover letter that includes your skills and experiences as they relate to each of the basic qualifications. Review of applications will begin on March 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://surgery.smhs.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/123887 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-eligible or board-certified in general surgery and surgical critical care at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated excellence in teaching as evidenced by teaching evaluations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated excellence in research as evidenced by scholarly publications or works in progress? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellence in clinical care as evidenced by experience, fellowships, and references? Yes No * Are you eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129363": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Admissions",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Director, Admissions Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director, Admissions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The Assistant Director, Admissions is responsible for coordinating and supporting recruitment, admissions, and enrollment activities for multiple undergraduate and graduate health sciences programs. This position serves as a primary point of contact for prospective students throughout the admissions process and works collaboratively with faculty, academic leadership, and university offices to ensure a seamless applicant experience. The Assistant Director, Admissions promotes the institution’s health sciences programs, supports enrollment goals, and assists in the implementation of recruitment strategies designed to attract a diverse and highly qualified student population. Key Responsibilities and Duties Recruitment and Outreach Develop and implement recruitment strategies for undergraduate and graduate health sciences programs. Represent the institution at recruitment events, college fairs, virtual information sessions, open houses, and professional conferences. Build and maintain relationships with prospective students, academic advisors, community colleges, healthcare organizations, and partner institutions. Conduct outreach to prospective undergraduate and graduate students through phone, email, virtual meetings, and in-person interactions. Respond to inquiries from prospective students in a timely and professional manner. Assist in developing recruitment materials, presentations, and digital communications. Support strategic enrollment initiatives to increase applicant yield and program visibility. Admissions and Application Management Review and process applications for assigned undergraduate and graduate programs. Evaluate applicant materials for completeness, eligibility, and compliance with institutional and program-specific requirements. Monitor applicant progress and communicate application status, admissions requirements, deadlines, and next steps. Coordinate with faculty admissions committees and program directors regarding applicant review and admissions decisions. Maintain accurate admissions records and applicant data within the admissions CRM and student information systems. Applicant Support and Customer Service Provide accurate and timely information regarding program requirements, admissions criteria, tuition, prerequisite coursework, and enrollment procedures. Provide individualized guidance to applicants throughout the admissions process. Support admitted students through onboarding and transition activities to improve enrollment yield and student engagement. Deliver high-quality customer service while maintaining confidentiality and professionalism. Collaboration and Administrative Support Work collaboratively with academic departments, advisors, and faculty. Participate in admissions committee meetings and recruitment planning activities. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, accreditation standards, and applicable federal and state regulations. Performs other duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Hybrid working environment with both in office and remote work each week. Periodic local travel for recruitment activities. Occasional evening and weekend work required during peak recruitment periods and special events. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications Experience working with diverse student populations. Ability to travel locally and work occasional evenings and weekends for recruitment events. Experience in admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, higher education, or related field. Experience working with student information systems, CRM platforms, and application management systems preferred. Experience working with health sciences or healthcare-related academic programs. Knowledge of higher education admissions processes. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Excellent verbal communication skills. Strong customer service orientation and relationship-building skills. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Cultural competency and commitment to inclusive recruitment practices. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Hiring Range $47,073.26 - $64,771.35 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: School of Medicine and Health Sciences (SMHS) Family Enrollment Services Sub-Family Admissions Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 2 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Mon-Fri 9:00am-5:30pm Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014475 Job Open Date: 10/15/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current GW employee? Yes No * If you are a current staff or research employee at The George Washington University, have you successfully completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)? The Introductory Employment Period (IEP) at George Washington University for non-faculty benefitted staff and research positions lasts for 90 days from the hire date into the position. Employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete. Yes No Not Applicable (Not a GW employee in a benefit eligible position) * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118861": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology)",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on March 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002496 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Nephrology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 7/1/2025-6/30/2026 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with the George Washington University, seeks full-time academic nephrologists for its Division of Kidney Diseases & Hypertension in the Department of Medicine. These non-tenure track appointments will be made at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience, with the possibility of additional incentives if eligible. The Division of Kidney Diseases and Hypertension at the George Washington University School of Medicine has a long and distinguished history of remarkable achievements in scientific discovery, education, and clinical care of kidney disease. The division is ranked by the US News and World Report, and it has several NIH -funded faculty members. These positions are expected to begin as early as July 1, 2025. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing excellent clinical care, maintaining an active research program, and participating in clinical teaching. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board certified/eligible in Nephrology and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. A record of academic excellence, as demonstrated by clinical experience, publications, evaluations, and/or references, is required. Advertised Salary: $240,000.00 to $265,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on March 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/renal Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118117 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified/eligible in Nephrology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have a record of academic excellence, as demonstrated by clinical experience, publications, evaluations and/or references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
