    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/126564": {
      "title": "Lighting Engineer",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Lighting Engineer Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Lighting Engineer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. This role will report to the Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington DC. Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: Events & Venues at the George Washington University (a department in the Division of Safety & Operations) designs, produces, and manages events on the Foggy Bottom Campus. We provide services to a broad spectrum of clients both in the community and outside of the community. We provide spaces for our students, faculty, staff, and guests to host events, meetings, and gatherings. We highlight university traditions, produce memorable guest speaker events, and coordinate many other activities unique to our campus with local, national, and international acclaim. Our record of excellence, support, and cooperation is one that we are proud of. Events & Venues are seeking temporary Lighting Engineers. This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. The responsibilities for this position include but are not limited to: -Operate lights for rehearsals and shows -Design shows as needs arise -Read, edit and update lighting plots -Maintain and supervise maintenance of Lisner Auditorium’s lighting equipment and inventory -Report on the status of show needs and maintenance needs to the Venue Manager -Supervise crew on lighting calls (only for Inter II and Master categories) -Assist other departments (Sound, Audio Visual, carpentry, rigging, etc.) as needed under the direction of the Venue Manager -Work with and supervise other GWU venues and students with their lighting needs -Recommend upgrades and improvements in lighting needs for the auditorium and other GWU venues -Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 2 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Proficiency in VectorWorks or AutoCAD, Microsoft Office, and other basic computer software programs. II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Safety and Operation Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: Varies; approximately 20 hours per week Hiring Range $32.42 - $55.90 Work Schedule: Varies; Monday-Sunday, Evenings Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status On-campus (in person) Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: This role will be part-time with an on-call reporting status. Additionally, this role will require working occasional nights and weekends. This role will report to the Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington DC. Position Type: Posting Number: T001129 Job Open Date: 06/16/2026 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: No Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your expected hourly range? (Open Ended Question) * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129584": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will be on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Application procedure: To be considered, applicants must apply through the GW employment portal and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae (CV). Cover Letter, including the names of three references. Sample publication or presentation, demonstrating scholarly research and/or professional contributions. Sample classroom evaluations or course evaluation summaries, demonstrating graduate-level teaching experience. Other Documents: Licensure status statement and sample teaching syllabus. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002674 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/2027-06/30/2030 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Program in Professional Psychology seeks an Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology in a non-tenure accruing contract position to begin as early as July 1, 2027 for an initial 3-year renewable appointment on a 12-month basis. The Program in Professional Psychology emphasizes psychodynamic orientation and has areas of emphasis including child and adolescent psychology, psychological assessment, multicultural and globally focused approaches, group psychotherapy, and community interventions. The Program values diversity and inclusion. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities in the program may include doctoral level coursework in psychology, such as applied statistics, cognitive-affective theory, or applied research design along with clinical courses such as psychotherapy or assessment supervision. The successful candidate will perform service to the program including student advising, mentoring, clinical training (practica), supervision, and other activities. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of research. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have: An earned doctoral degree in clinical or counseling psychology from a program accredited by the American Psychological Association by date of appointment. Licensure or license eligibility as a psychologist in the District of Columbia. Teaching experience at the graduate level including supervision of clinical work. A commitment to scholarly research and discovery as evidenced by a record of scholarly presentations and/or publications. Advertised Salary: $105,000-120,000 Other Benefits: The successful candidate will be eligible for participation in GW’s comprehensive employee benefits package, including medical insurance. For more information on GW’s benefits visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Review of applications will be on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Application procedure: To be considered, applicants must apply through the GW employment portal and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae (CV). Cover Letter, including the names of three references. Sample publication or presentation, demonstrating scholarly research and/or professional contributions. Sample classroom evaluations or course evaluation summaries, demonstrating graduate-level teaching experience. Other Documents: Licensure status statement and sample teaching syllabus. Department Link: http://psyd.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129153 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Sample Publications Other Documents Refer to Special Instructions to Applicants Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctoral degree in clinical or counseling psychology from a program accredited by the American Psychological Association, or will you have completed this degree by the date of appointment? Yes No * Are you currently licensed, or are you eligible for licensure, as a psychologist in the District of Columbia? Yes No * Do you have teaching experience at the graduate level, including supervision of clinical work? Yes No * Do you have a commitment to scholarly research and discovery, as evidenced by a record of scholarly presentations and/or publications? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128823": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Economics Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a current CV, (3) one or at most two research papers, (4) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (5) teaching evaluations (if available), (6) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002657 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Economics Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University’s Department of Economics invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position beginning as early as Fall 2027. We seek applicants specializing in applied microeconomics who demonstrate strong potential for scholarly achievement and excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active research program and contribute to the intellectual and professional life of the Department and University. Teaching responsibilities will include courses for undergraduate and graduate students in the Economics Department. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in economics with a primary focus on applied microeconomics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or complete all requirements for the Ph.D. by the date of appointment. Advertised Salary: $140,000-$155,000 Other Benefits: Health Benefits: GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a current CV, (3) one or at most two research papers, (4) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (5) teaching evaluations (if available), (6) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Department Link: https://economics.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128624 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
