    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/119051": {
      "title": "Group Fitness Instructor II",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Group Fitness Instructor II Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Group Fitness Instructor II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details I. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION Job Description Summary: Group Fitness Instructors lead group-based instruction for a variety of formats; at least one class/week on a regular weekly schedule. General responsibilities include: Provide a safe, friendly, and fun environment for GW student, staff, faculty, and community participants; Demonstrate instructional skills, strategies, and knowledge of group fitness components; Maintain general organization of studio equipment and technology; Know, follow and enforce Campus Recreation policies and procedures; Attend meetings and continuous training opportunities as provided. · Applicants must be certified in group fitness, Yoga, Pilates, Barre, or another relevant format Minimum Qualifications: Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: II. POSITION INFORMATION Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Student Affairs Family Sub-Family Stream Level Full-Time/Part-Time: Hours Per Week: 7, varies Hiring Range 28.00 Work Schedule: Monday - Sunday Position Designation: Employee Onsite Status Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Position Type: Posting Number: T000679 Job Open Date: 09/10/2024 Job Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Applicant Review Will Commence On: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role is a GWTemps role. GWTemps is the internal temporary agency at GW. As a university employee, you are eligible to apply to internal university postings if you ever wanted to transition from a temporary role to a permanent role. Since this is a temporary position, this role is ineligible for university benefits, to include, annual/vacation leave, university and federal holiday pay, university closure/administrative pay, retirement benefits, healthcare insurance, etc. Do you acknowledge this information? Yes No * What is your hourly rate expectation? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
