    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129596": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor &amp; Director, Community Counseling Services Center",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Clinical Assistant Professor &amp; Director, Community Counseling Services Center Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Assistant Professor & Director, Community Counseling Services Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. How to Apply: Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Please submit an online application. Applicant must include the following information when applying for this position: (1) letter of application including a statement of qualifications in relation to listed areas of expertise and department mission; a statement regarding the applicant’s philosophy of teaching; and a research statement. (2) current curriculum vitae; (3) copies of graduate transcripts; (4) evidence of teaching activity and teaching effectiveness (e.g. peer or student evaluations); and, (5) contact information from three references Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002682 Academic Title: Clinical Assistant Professor & Director, Community Counseling Services Center Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Clinical Assistant Professor & Director, Community Counseling Services Center Discipline Education Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Time-Limited Appointment (provide appt period) - 01/01/2027-06/30/2030 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 01/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University’s Department of Counseling and Human Development is seeking applicants for a non-tenure-accruing specialized faculty position at the Clinical Assistant Professor level, beginning as early as Spring 2027. The Counseling and Human Development Department has a strong identity in diversity, disability, and human development research. The Department espouses an anti-oppressive stance as it engages in its mission of teaching, research, and service. The Clinical Assistant Professor and Director of the Community Counseling Services Center-Foggy Bottom will provide comprehensive oversight for the Community Counseling Services Center, a counseling training clinic wherein students across counseling programs provide mental health services to members of the community. This 12-month appointment includes teaching across programs within the Department of Counseling and Human Development. Additionally, this role includes the administrative duties of the Community Counseling Services Center-Foggy Bottom, including, overseeing clinic operations, ensuring quality care is provided to students, management of student workers and supervisors, and providing clinic supervision. Service responsibilities include engaging in departmental, school, and university committees as needed. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Clinical Oversight ● Provide clinical oversight of clinic staff, engaging in crisis management as needed (available if needed during clinic hours M-Thursday 11-8pm) ● Provide leadership to clinic staff, promoting a collaborative, supportive, and professional clinic environment. ● Collaborate with Assistant Directors to ensure appropriateness of clients for student clinicians ● Support marketing of the clinic to ensure viability of the clinic ● Integrate clinical, administrative, and supervisory responsibilities to ensure the clinic’s smooth operation. ● Foster a learning environment for counseling interns, supporting their growth in both theoretical and applied aspects of clinical practice. ● Manage clinic administrative processes, including orientation, policies, & procedures ● Maintain up-to-date knowledge of accreditation and compliance requirements, ensuring clinic meets all legal and ethical standards. ● Maintain accurate referral list for clients’ and counseling interns’ use ● Assist in adapting yearly training curriculum for counseling students and supervisors. ● Maintain and manage technology systems associated with the clinical training program, including the electronic health record and the video-recording capacities of the CCSC , and ensuring the confidentiality of all client records, recordings, and documents. ● Track and apply payments from client sessions ● Potential provision of clinical supervision for up to up to six interns each semester Faculty Responsibilities ● Teach graduate level clinical counseling courses (e.g. Interview skills, theories of counseling, marriage and family counseling) ● Engage in the accreditation related Clinical Training Committee activities ● Engage in departmental meetings and committees Minimum Qualifications: Basic Qualifications. All applicants must have: ● Doctorate from a CACREP accredited Counselor Education Program by date of appointment. ● Clinical experience in mental health, rehabilitation, or school counseling. ● Experience in providing clinical supervision and training to interns or students. Advertised Salary: 80,000-95,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits . Other Information: The George Washington University has a strong commitment to recruiting faculty of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the university with a wide variety of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. The Department of Counseling and Human Development houses three master’s degree programs, several certificate programs, and a PhD in Counseling. The Rehabilitation Counseling program is ranked third in the US, according to US News and World Report. The department has partnerships with many field sites in the metropolitan DC area where its students can complete practicum and internship experiences. Special Instructions to Applicants: How to Apply: Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Please submit an online application. Applicant must include the following information when applying for this position: (1) letter of application including a statement of qualifications in relation to listed areas of expertise and department mission; a statement regarding the applicant’s philosophy of teaching; and a research statement. (2) current curriculum vitae; (3) copies of graduate transcripts; (4) evidence of teaching activity and teaching effectiveness (e.g. peer or student evaluations); and, (5) contact information from three references Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129499 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript Names and Contact Information for References Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will you have a doctorate from a CACREP accredited Counselor Education Program by date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have clinical experience in mental health, rehabilitation, or school counseling? Yes No * Do you have experience in providing clinical supervision and training to interns or students? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129464": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: a cover letter describing interest in and qualifications for the position; a curriculum vitae including a detailed description of teaching experience, service experience, and scholarly publications including those related to biology education; a 2-page statement of teaching philosophy; copies of official student evaluations from past courses taught; and the names and contact information for three referees who can comment on your classroom instruction. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002665 Academic Title: Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology Rank: Teaching Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Basic Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Special Service, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 08/01/27-05/31/30 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences at The George Washington University invites applicants for a position as a Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology to begin as soon as Fall 2027. This is a full-time, renewable, Specialized Service contract position with a course load of 3 courses per semester (Fall and Spring). The initial renewable appointment period will be for 3 years. Because this is a teaching position, there are no research expectations, but the candidate will be required to contribute some effort towards service for the University and maintain knowledge in the discipline sufficient to support teaching. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The primary responsibilities of the candidate will comprise the design, delivery, and supervision of undergraduate courses associated with our non-majors Introductory Biology sequence to offer content in areas such as cellular biology, microbiology, nutrition, physiology, and evolution to multiple large lecture sections each semester. The candidate will manage and coordinate labs associated with the non-majors Introductory Biology lectures while collaborating with our teaching faculty, laboratory managers, graduate teaching assistants, and undergraduate teaching assistants to ensure a high-quality educational experience that prepares undergraduate students for advanced coursework and to be scientifically literate citizens. There may also be opportunities to rotate into majors Introductory Biology and/or an upper-division course related to the candidate’s area of expertise depending on departmental needs. In addition, the candidate will have the opportunity to collaborate with educational consultants and instructional technology specialists through the Center for Teaching Excellence ( https://library.gwu.edu/about-center-teaching-excellence ) to receive professional development in evidence-based pedagogy, course (re-)design, active learning, effective assessment practices, etc. Office space will be provided in Bell Hall, where the teaching labs for our Introductory Biology courses are housed. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have completed a Ph.D. in Biological Sciences or related discipline by the time the appointment begins and must have experience teaching a combination of lecture or laboratory courses as instructor of record at the university level. Advertised Salary: $75,000-$80,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits . Other Information: Questions about this position may be directed to the Chair of the search committee, Dr. J. Aidan Manubay at jmanubay@gwu.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload the following documents: a cover letter describing interest in and qualifications for the position; a curriculum vitae including a detailed description of teaching experience, service experience, and scholarly publications including those related to biology education; a 2-page statement of teaching philosophy; copies of official student evaluations from past courses taught; and the names and contact information for three referees who can comment on your classroom instruction. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage for candidates advancing to the second stage of the process. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, pending final budgetary approval. Department Link: https://biology.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/129028 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Interest Names and Contact Information for References Course Evaluations or Summaries Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD in Biology or a related discipline, or will you have completed the requirements for the PhD by the time of appointment? Yes No * Can you demonstrate experience teaching a combination of lecture and laboratory courses as the instructor of record at the university level? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128874": {
      "title": "Senior Trades Helper",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Trades Helper Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Trades Helper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: Facilities, Buildings & Grounds ( FBG ) Life Safety Shop is seeking a Senior Trades Helper with excellent customer service skills and the ability to physically perform job duties, including: climbing, balancing, stooping, kneeling, lifting, carrying, pushing or pulling a variety of equipment. Carries out special jobs or emergency call as assigned. This position will receive on-the-job training in the building trade to which assigned. Ability to work flexible schedule and on-call / rotating weekends. FBG is a part of GW’s Facilities, Planning and Construction Management Division, which maintains GW’s property and grounds on all three campuses. Employees at GWU are offered a competitive salary, excellent benefits package, general retirement savings options that include university contributions and matching contributions, generous Annual and Sick leave benefits plus many more. For more information about GW benefits, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits Reporting to the Fire Alarm Shop Supervisor, the Senior Trades Helper supports the Fire/Life Safety team efforts in Emergency Generator Preventive Maintenance, Fire Alarm System Inspection, Testing and Repair, and Sprinkler Systems Inspection, Testing, and Repair. The Responsibilities of a Senior Trades Helper include, but are not limited to: Assist with and /or perform Generator PM Testing, Visual Inspections, Logging Usage/Run Times, Topping of Fluids as needed, and responding to related emergencies. Assist with and /or perform Fire Alarm Servicing of Battery Replacements, Detector Cleaning or Replacement, Testing Fire Alarm Systems across campus marking deficiencies and scheduling best repair and retest times with customers. Overseeing projects to ensure integrity of Fire Alarm systems is maintained. Responding to Emergency Calls and Building Trouble signals within a reasonable time frame. Assist with and/or perform Wet/Dry Sprinkler Visual Inspections of Valves across Campus, Testing of Drum Drips, Fire Pumps, Dry System Components, Wet System Components, Jockey Pumps and any integrated Fire Alarm monitoring equipment. Responding to related emergencies. Ensuring Buildings maintain Fire Safety Code Requirements. May serve in or represent the Supervisor at various meetings that may impact the unit. Enhances professional knowledge and skills by attending job-related seminars, workshops, and conferences and/or reviewing published literature. Performs other work related duties as requested. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED , or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Ability to physically perform job duties, including: climbing, balancing, stooping, kneeling, lifting, carrying, pushing or pulling a variety of equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Nicet Fire Alarm Systems Lvl.1 (strongly desired) Nicet Fire Alarm Systems Lvl.2 (preferred) Nicet Sprinkler Inspect & Test (willingness to obtain within a period of time) Intermediate computer skills with Windows 7, Microsoft Office Suite, and various web browsing software platforms. Proficient with computerized tools and testing equipment. PERSONAL CHARACTERISTICS Looking for an individual with the following characteristics: Commitment to GW’s values Intellectual, professional and a person of integrity Honest, with the highest ethical standards Passionate, collaborative, strategic, and smart with a hands-on, roll-up-the-sleeves orientation Ability to work independently. Self-starter; hard worker. Takes initiative; very high energy Personally accountable. Assumes ownership, control and accountability for all areas of responsibility and commitments made to others; Sincere, open, and direct communicator. Puts organizational interests above self- interests and is comfortable expressing candid opinions Highest levels of responsiveness Combination of strong intellect that is combined with a practical and realistic common sense understanding of how to get things done Ability to demonstrate initiative, a strong desire to succeed and exert the extraordinary effort often required Ability to work in a fast-paced, high growth, entrepreneurial environment Ability to work with faculty and staff in a respectful way Establish trust and credibility with institutional leadership and across the University Seeks “win-win” solutions to help foster continued integration and collaboration Flexible and receptive to change; and A positive “can-do” attitude. Must be responsive to after-hours calls from associates and other colleagues. Hiring Range $20.42 - $26.47 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Safety and Operation Family Safety and Facilities Sub-Family General Trades Stream Service and Support Level Level 1 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: 7:00 AM to 4:00 PM Monday- Friday to include a Holiday, after-hours, Overnight and Weekend Rotating schedule Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Essential onsite Telework: No Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014474 Job Open Date: 09/18/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)? (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
